My understanding is that setting "minbucket" to anything higher than 1 is
only for saving time in the computations.  Setting minbucket=1 gives the
most exhaustive search through the collections of possible trees.  For your
example, I'd stay with minbucket=1.

For all their similarities, tree and rpart are different in a few places.
At the very least the (default) splitting criteria are different.

Just my $0.02...

