> i am using  version Splus 61. on Windows and Visual C++ version 6.0
> 
> I am trying to create a dll file . I am using the inbuilt C  function
> for quick sort  defined in C ++ as follows:
> void qsort( void *base, size_t num, size_t width, int (__cdecl *compare
> )(const void *elem1, const void *elem2 ) );
> I am using the example they have in the C ++ help files for quick
> sort.It runs fine in C++,but when I try to build a dll file it gives the
> following error
> 
>  error C2664: 'qsort' : cannot convert parameter 4 from 'int (const void
> *,const void *)' to 'int (__cdecl *)(const void *,const void *)'
>  How can I modify my function protoype to  handle this?

The tools Insightful supply to make DLLs under S-PLUS 6.1 make DLLs with 
stdcall linkage.  So you need to declare your comparison routine as
cdecl.  Here's an example from the nnet library (in C):

static int
#if( defined(WIN32) && defined(SPLUS_VERSION) && SPLUS_VERSION >= 6000 )
__cdecl
#endif
Zcompar(const Sdata *a, const Sdata *b)

which does work with those tools (I use CHAPTER -m).

