Date: Tue, 04 Feb 2003 10:16:34 -0500
Subject: Hmisc and Design Libraries for S-Plus 2000
Message-ID: <20030204101634.079eeaaf.fharrell@virginia.edu>

Major updates to the Hmisc and Design libraries are available for S-Plus 2000 
at http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat/s/library/splus2000 .  These will 
likely be the last versions for S-Plus 2000.  Changes to the libraries are 
documented in http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat/s/library/common .  The 
most major change in the Design library is the implementation of weights for 
binary and ordinal logistic regression.  Many new functions have been added to 
Hmisc since the last binary for S-Plus 2000 was produced, and many more 
functions were enhanced or had bug fixes.  The most significant of these is 
perhaps extensive enhancements to summary.formula and the development of 
aregImpute for flexible multiple imputation. 

Thanks to Eric Bissonette of U. Virginia for his work in creating the binary 
distributions.
