From: sundar.dorai-raj at pdf.com (Sundar Dorai-Raj)
Date: Thu, 06 Feb 2003 10:17:18 -0600
Subject: Re: extract variance components in LME
References: <20030206140200.64117.qmail@web41304.mail.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <3E428A8E.20901@pdf.com>

Karin,

Karin Groothuis-Oudshoorn wrote:
> Hello,
>
>
>
> I want to analyse a model using the function lme. It is a simple model.
> with one random effect due to persons. Especially I am interested in the
> variance estimate of the random effect due to persons. This estimate is
> displayed then printing the fitobject (let me call this object fitlme).
> But how can I extract it from the fitobject (to use it in another
> function)? For the variance estimate of the residual this is
> straightforward, namely fitlme$sigma.
>
>
>
> The estimate of the variance due to persons is calculated somehow with
> fitlme$modelStruct, but I can not figure out how. Does someone has a
> suggestion?

Here's a script that will do it:

extract.stdev <- function(object) {
  struct <- object$modelStruct$reStruct
  sigma <- object$sigma
  Var <- rev(sapply(struct, as.matrix))
  labels <- sapply(seq(Var), function(x, names)
  paste(rev(names[1:x]), collapse = " %in% "), names = names(Var))
  Sdev <- c(sqrt(Var) * sigma, sigma)
  names(Sdev) <- c(labels, "Residual")
  Sdev
}

where data.class(object)=="lme".

I can't guarantee it will work in all situations if you have some funky 
group structure, but it's a start.

Sundar

