From andy_liaw at merck.com  Sat Feb  8 18:27:03 2003
From: andy_liaw at merck.com (Liaw, Andy)
Date: Sat, 08 Feb 2003 13:27:03 -0500
Subject: Re: Fisher's protected testing procedure
Message-ID: <3A822319EB35174CA3714066D590DCD534BC69@usrymx25.merck.com>

The 
context in which I've heard the term refers to the fact that the Fisher's LSD is 
only carried out when the overall F-test is significant; i.e., the procedure is 
`protected' by the overall F-test.  If you perform the LSD comparisons 
regardless of whether the overall F-test is significant, that would be 
`unprotected'.

 

HTH,

Andy

