From paulda at BATTELLE.ORG  Wed Feb 12 14:29:25 2003
From: paulda at BATTELLE.ORG (Paul, David A)
Date: Wed, 12 Feb 2003 09:29:25 -0500
Subject: Confirmed Splus 6.1 Bug
Message-ID: <CFA6739DD532764AA51E7459970BF0E205D0AACE@ns-bco-mse3.im.battelle.org>

Last week I contacted technical support at Insightful and passed along
some of my code.  Splus 6.1 kept generating strange errors (among other
things) when I tried to perform a stratified linear regression analysis,
where the stratifying variable was of type "factor".

Insightful was able to reproduce the problem, so it wasn't due to my
operating system, and it does not appear to be a platform-dependent bug.
Insightful has promised to have a bug fix implemented when 6.2 is
released.  Here is a partial listing of the response email that 
Insightful sent to me, confirming the bug:

Problem Description:
  SPLUS: lm(Weight ~ Mileage + Mileage:Type - 1, data=fuel.frame)
  This results in errors (invalid frame number and problem in 
  model.matrix.default) and then ""Engine connection failure - shutting 
  down S-PLUS recommended". The bug appears to be if factor term and 
  intercept are removed from formula.

The following commands run okay:

> lm(Weight ~ Mileage*Type-1, data=fuel.frame)
> lm(Weight ~ Mileage + Type + Mileage:Type-1, data=fuel.frame)

but if you remove "Type":

> lm(Weight ~ Mileage + Mileage:Type -1, data=fuel.frame)

then you get error(s) and S-PLUS does not function properly and/or 
crashes.  The errors from running the above "bug" command in a script 
are:

#1  Problem: Invalid frame number (0) in set_frame 
    Use traceback() to see the call stack

#2  Problem in model.matrix.default(Terms, m, contrasts..: Internal 
        error: predicted 5 columns for Mileage:Type, got 6 Error during 
        wrapup: Invalid frame number (0) in set_frame

#3  Problem in model.matrix.default(Terms, m, contrasts..: Internal 
        error: predicted 5 columns for Mileage:Type, got 6 
        Use traceback() to see the call stack

Trying to issue any command in the commands window results in an
error:

> objects()
Engine connection failure - shutting down S-PLUS recommended

Exiting S-PLUS results in the error message box:

"SPLUS.exe has generated errors and will be closed by Windows. 
You will need to restart the program. An error log is being created."

The problem seems to be removing BOTH the factor term and the 
intercept.  The following runs okay ("Type" removed):

> lm(Weight ~ Mileage + Mileage:Type, data=fuel.frame)

But if you then remove the intercept (-1) as illustrated above, 
errors occur.

I have not yet tried to perform stratified regression using 
stratifying variables of type = numeric (using, say 0-1 coding) so
I cannot say that all stratified regression models in which the main 
stratifying effect and intercept are removed result in errors.  
Perhaps someone from the S community could inform the listserv of 
their experiences?  It would also be helpful to know if similar 
function calls in R result in errors.

Respectfully,

  David Paul, Ph.D.
  Battelle Memorial Institute
  505 King Avenue
  Columbus, OH  43201
  614.424.3176

