It fails even in S-PLUS 3.4 but works in R (1.6.2), with an NA coefficient.

However, what do you think this model means?  Why should weight depend on
mileage, with no intercept?  It's nonsensical.  Maybe 1/mileage depends on
weight ....

What you appear to want is a model with no intercepts and different slopes
per group.  Why then do you have a main effect in it?  It makes sense (but
not in this example) to use

lm(Weight ~ Mileage:Type-1, data=fuel.frame)

and that does work.  That the `bug' has been ar ound for so long without
apparently causing any problems suggests that it is not occuring in
real-life models.

