> How about the following:
>               r <- c(rep("z", length(z)), rep("y", length(y)))
>               rank(c(z, y))[r == "y"] - rank(y)

Which simplifies (rather more transparently also) to:
rank(c(z, y))[-(1:length(z))] - rank(y)

This is by far the best solution (taking into account the Subject:
line), although it does not scale quite as well as my approx() based
solution (when the vectors get to length greater than a few thousand).

We haven't heard from the original poser of the question to indicate
which solution is most appropriate for the 'real' problem.  Hint. Hint!

