Thanks to Herb Root, Leonid Gibiansky, Jean Adams, Marc Schwartz and Jim
Pratt for their quick responses and for sharing their processes for copying
graphs to Word.
The suggestions (in the order received) were to:

 Use an intermediate drawing program such as Corel draw for touching
up graphs.

Use copy/paste special

Avoid the need for cropping by adjusting the margins in S-Plus using the
graphical parameter mar.

export to a Windows metafile format

Jim Pratt provided the command he uses to export to wmf.

Using
trellis.device(graphsheet, format='WMF',width=9,height=6,print.background=""
file='plot2##.wmf',color.scheme='Trellis black on white',orientation='landscape'),
a customization of Jim's command, seems to work.
