>From ?is.na:

REQUIRED ARGUMENTS:
x       an S-PLUS object, which should be logical, numeric, or complex.

WARNING:
This is always FALSE when x is of mode "character".

You should use == "NA" if x is character. As in:

> vec <- letters[1:5]
> vec[4] <- NA
> vec == "NA"
